{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba ../native-source/raft.go | sed -n '1083,1101p'; nl -ba ../native-source/api.go | sed -n '806,828p'; nl -ba ../native-source/config.go | sed -n '160,177p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1083\t// quorumSize is used to return the quorum size. This must only be called on\n  1084\t// the main thread.\n  1085\t// TODO: revisit usage\n  1086\tfunc (r *Raft) quorumSize() int {\n  1087\t\tvoters := 0\n  1088\t\tfor _, server := range r.configurations.latest.Servers {\n  1089\t\t\tif server.Suffrage == Voter {\n  1090\t\t\t\tvoters++\n  1091\t\t\t}\n  1092\t\t}\n  1093\t\treturn voters/2 + 1\n  1094\t}\n  1095\t\n  1096\t// restoreUserSnapshot is used to manually consume an external snapshot, such\n  1097\t// as if restoring from a backup. We will use the current Raft configuration,\n  1098\t// not the one from the snapshot, so that we can restore into a new cluster. We\n  1099\t// will also use the higher of the index of the snapshot, or the current index,\n  1100\t// and then add 1 to that, so we force a new state with a hole in the Raft log,\n  1101\t// so that the snapshot will be sent to followers and used for any new joiners.\n   806\t// An optional timeout can be provided to limit the amount of time we wait\n   807\t// for the command to be started. This must be run on the leader or it\n   808\t// will fail.\n   809\t//\n   810\t// If the node discovers it is no longer the leader while applying the command,\n   811\t// it will return ErrLeadershipLost. There is no way to guarantee whether the\n   812\t// write succeeded or failed in this case. For example, if the leader is\n   813\t// partitioned it can't know if a quorum of followers wrote the log to disk. If\n   814\t// at least one did, it may survive into the next leader's term.\n   815\t//\n   816\t// If a user snapshot is restored while the command is in-flight, an\n   817\t// ErrAbortedByRestore is returned. In this case the write effectively failed\n   818\t// since its effects will not be present in the FSM after the restore.\n   819\tfunc (r *Raft) Apply(cmd []byte, timeout time.Duration) ApplyFuture {\n   820\t\treturn r.ApplyLog(Log{Data: cmd}, timeout)\n   821\t}\n   822\t\n   823\t// ApplyLog performs Apply but takes in a Log directly. The only values\n   824\t// currently taken from the submitted Log are Data and Extensions. See\n   825\t// Apply for details on error cases.\n   826\tfunc (r *Raft) ApplyLog(log Log, timeout time.Duration) ApplyFuture {\n   827\t\tmetrics.IncrCounter([]string{\"raft\", \"apply\"}, 1)\n   828\t\n   160\t\t// Due to random staggering, may be delayed as much as 2x this value.\n   161\t\tCommitTimeout time.Duration\n   162\t\n   163\t\t// MaxAppendEntries controls the maximum number of append entries\n   164\t\t// to send at once. We want to strike a balance between efficiency\n   165\t\t// and avoiding waste if the follower is going to reject because of\n   166\t\t// an inconsistent log.\n   167\t\tMaxAppendEntries int\n   168\t\n   169\t\t// BatchApplyCh indicates whether we should buffer applyCh\n   170\t\t// to size MaxAppendEntries. This enables batch log commitment,\n   171\t\t// but breaks the timeout guarantee on Apply. Specifically,\n   172\t\t// a log can be added to the applyCh buffer but not actually be\n   173\t\t// processed until after the specified timeout.\n   174\t\tBatchApplyCh bool\n   175\t\n   176\t\t// If we are a member of a cluster, and RemovePeer is invoked for the\n   177\t\t// local node, then we forget all peers and transition into the follower state.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The commitment and lease paths filter by voter eligibility, but `VerifyLeader` registers with every replication worker, including nonvoters. I’m selecting a stronger discriminator: whether an isolated old leader can return verification success after the remaining voters have elected a replacement and committed a command. That would test authority validity beyond the registration asymmetry.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > prepare_verify.py <<'PY'\nimport json,jsonschema\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v3.json'))\nfor a in m['activities']: a.pop('behavior_ids',None)\nfor f in m['facts']:\n for k in ('established_by','consumed_by'): f.pop(k,None)\nspecs=[('src_verify_api','api.go',880,903,'interface_statement'),('src_verify_register','raft.go',963,987,'code_observation'),('src_verify_finish','raft.go',848,870,'code_observation'),('src_verify_count','future.go',272,293,'code_observation'),('src_notify_all','replication.go',98,111,'code_observation'),('src_heartbeat_support','replication.go',388,440,'code_observation'),('src_replication_members','raft.go',580,645,'code_observation'),('src_voter_quorum','raft.go',1083,1094,'code_observation'),('src_voter_lease','raft.go',1032,1081,'code_observation'),('src_member_roles','configuration.go',8,59,'interface_statement'),('src_config_transition','configuration.go',194,306,'code_observation'),('src_config_stability','raft.go',647,663,'code_observation'),('src_config_activation','raft.go',1200,1240,'code_observation'),('src_nonvoter_api','api.go',959,975,'interface_statement')]\nsources=[dict(id=i,file=f,start_line=a,end_line=b,kind=k) for i,f,a,b,k in specs]\ndef b(i,act,owner,ctx,trig,ss,**kw): return dict(id=i,primary_activity=act,execution_owner=owner,protocol_context=ctx,trigger=trig,source_ids=ss,**kw)\nm['behaviors'] += [\nb('B_verify_register','A2','Leader main loop','One verifyFuture with latest configuration voter threshold','Public VerifyLeader arrives with quorumSize zero',['src_verify_register','src_voter_quorum','src_replication_members','src_verify_api'],reads=['Latest configuration and all replState workers'],writes=['votes=1; quorumSize=voters/2+1','Register future in each replication worker notify map'],external_effects=['Immediate nil for single-voter quorum; otherwise trigger every worker heartbeat'],existing_protections=['Registration serialized in main loop'],unknowns=['Registration has no suffrage filter even though threshold counts voters; significance requires actual authority history.']),\nb('B_peer_notify','A2','Per-peer heartbeat or replication worker','Verification future registered in that worker notify map','Successful transport heartbeat completion or other replication notification',['src_heartbeat_support','src_notify_all','src_match_update','src_snapshot_match'],reads=['Heartbeat Success or successful replication outcome','Worker pending notifications'],writes=['Clear worker notify map'],external_effects=['Call vote(leader) for each pending verification'],important_branches=['Heartbeat transport error does not call notifyAll','Heartbeat response Success=false votes negatively','Append/snapshot success also notifies verification'],unknowns=['Heartbeat does not test response term in this path; negative responses and lease remain protections.']),\nb('B_verify_count','A2','Replication worker under verifyFuture voteLock','Single verifyFuture and snapshotted threshold','vote(leader) from registered worker',['src_verify_count'],reads=['votes/quorumSize/notifyCh'],writes=['Increment affirmative count without peer identity or suffrage argument','Clear notifyCh after threshold or negative reply'],produces_fact_ids=['F_verify_threshold'],external_effects=['Send future to leader verifyCh'],important_branches=['Any negative reply notifies early','Ignore later votes after notifyCh nil'],existing_protections=['One delivery per future after threshold or negative outcome','Worker notify map is cleared per peer notification']),\nb('B_verify_finish','A2','Leader main loop','Previously registered verifyFuture returns on verifyCh','Verification completion notification',['src_verify_finish','src_verify_api'],consumes_fact_ids=['F_verify_threshold'],reads=['votes and quorumSize'],writes=['Remove future from leader and replication notify maps'],external_effects=['Return nil if count reaches threshold; otherwise ErrNotLeader and transition to follower'],unknowns=['No suffrage revalidation at this endpoint.','A successful count need not establish authority if contributing peer eligibility is insufficient; actual history is selected as next discriminator.']),\nb('B_member_activation','A4','Leader main loop','Stable previous configuration and current-term commitment','Configuration request selected from configurationChangeChIfStable',['src_config_stability','src_config_activation','src_config_transition','src_replication_members','src_commitment'],reads=['Current configuration and optional prevIndex'],writes=['Configuration log and latest configuration','Voter-only commitment map','Replication workers for all latest members'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Commitment map excludes nonvoters and preserves indexes only for retained voters','A2':'Replication map includes nonvoters and is the set used by verification registration'},existing_protections=['Wait for previous configuration and current-term entry commitment','Reject duplicate IDs/addresses and zero-voter result','Commitment ignores reports from IDs outside current voter map'],unknowns=['Membership persistence-error paths and generation transitions not resolved.']),\nb('B_lease_check','A2','Leader main loop','Current latest voter configuration and configured lease interval','Leader lease timer',['src_voter_lease','src_voter_quorum'],reads=['Only voter LastContact timestamps'],writes=['Follower state when voter contact count below quorum'],existing_protections=['Explicit suffrage filtering excludes nonvoter contacts'],unknowns=['Finite timer scheduling and configured timeout can allow an interval before stepdown; a candidate witness must retain this worker.'])]\nm['facts'].append(dict(id='F_verify_threshold',meaning='For this verifyFuture, its affirmative notification count, initialized with one self contribution, reached the voter-derived threshold and the future was enqueued for leader-loop completion. Notifications do not carry peer suffrage into vote(). This is counted support, not established continuing authority.',identity={'operation':'verifyFuture instance','threshold':'quorumSize captured at registration','context':'leader verification registration and notify maps'},validity_context='From affirmative threshold notification until leader-loop consumption; membership and authority validity are separate.',representation=['verifyFuture.votes','verifyFuture.quorumSize','verifyCh delivery'],durability='Volatile operation-local notification.',recovery='No recovery guarantee; futures belong to current process/leader context.',source_ids=['src_verify_count','src_verify_register','src_voter_quorum','src_verify_finish'],unknowns=['A legal history where only nonvoter support completes a stale leader verification has not been executed.','Negative responses, ordinary replication and lease stepdown can prevent the suspected endpoint.']))\nm['surfaces'].append(dict(entry_point='Raft.VerifyLeader',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B_verify_register','B_peer_notify','B_verify_count','B_verify_finish','B_lease_check'],reason='Mapped authority verification threshold and independent voter-only lease protection. Need a real election/command prefix to test whether nonvoter support can falsely validate old authority.',source_ids=['src_verify_api','src_verify_register','src_verify_finish','src_voter_lease'],high_consequence=True))\n# Leave the older commitment-membership surface deferred: this addition does not close its full transition question.\nq=dict(question='Can VerifyLeader return nil on a partitioned old leader after the remaining voters elected a higher-term replacement and completed a command before the verification invocation, while only a nonvoter remains reachable from the old leader?',importance='VerifyLeader is documented as ensuring continuing leadership and preventing stale FSM reads. A false positive after a newer leader has completed a write would invalidate that authority check; this question does not assume the application actually performs a stale read.',source_ids=[],participants=['Old leader','Two other voters','Nonvoter','Public API caller'],objects=['verifyFuture','Latest membership','Election term','Completed Apply command'],contexts=['Stable three-voter plus one-nonvoter configuration','Old leader separated from voting peers while nonvoter remains connected','New leader command completion precedes old VerifyLeader invocation','Lease and negative-response workers remain enabled'],event_paths=['Real bootstrap -> public AddVoter transitions -> stable configuration -> link partition -> replacement leader election -> successful Apply -> old VerifyLeader -> public future completion'],activity_classes=['A2','A4','A7'],behavior_ids=['B_verify_count','B_verify_finish'],fact_ids=['F_verify_threshold'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B_verify_register':'Initializes voter threshold and registers all replication workers.','B_peer_notify':'Actual positive/negative notification producers.','B_member_activation':'Produces stable voter/nonvoter membership through public changes.','B_lease_check':'Independent voter-only protection that must remain running in the witness.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Lease check counts only voters and eventually steps down an isolated leader.','A negative peer response can abort verification before affirmative count reaches threshold.','Commitment itself ignores nonvoter match indexes.'],unknowns=['The proposed real same-execution prefix and public verification endpoint remain to be executed.','The stale-read application consequence is excluded unless separately observed.','Different per-node timeouts must pass actual configuration validation and leave protective workers enabled.'],priority=3,trigger_rationale='Source shows voter-derived verification threshold combined with registration of all replication workers and identity-free vote increments. A source asymmetry alone is insufficient; select authority invalidation by an actual newer leader write as the discriminator.',disposition='ready_for_check',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')\nsel=set(q['behavior_ids'])|set(q['supporting_behavior_ids'])\nq['source_ids']=sorted(set(['src_verify_api']+m['facts'][-1]['source_ids']+sum([x['source_ids'] for x in m['behaviors'] if x['id'] in sel],[])))\nclaim=dict(id='O_verify_after_replacement',kind='obligation',concern='consensus_safety',description='VerifyLeader invoked on an old leader after a replacement leader in a strictly higher term has successfully completed Apply must not return success, while the old leader has not regained leadership and membership remains unchanged.',source_ids=['src_verify_api','src_verify_register','src_verify_finish','src_voter_quorum','src_member_roles'],scope=dict(description='Same-cluster authority check after a higher-term replacement leader completes a write before invocation; stable three-voter plus one-nonvoter membership and finite link partition, no process restart or Byzantine data.',assumptions=['A successful replacement Apply and higher term are observed before verification admission.','No membership change or old-leader re-election occurs during the observed interval.','All protocol workers including leader lease checks continue under configured legal timeouts.'],excluded=['Actual application stale read unless observed','General liveness or deadline claims','Reusing server identity or fabricating responses']),pending=[],grounding=dict(source_ids=['src_verify_register','src_verify_count','src_verify_finish','src_voter_lease','src_member_roles'],expectation_ids=['src_verify_api'],derivation='VerifyLeader documents ensuring the peer is still leader and preventing stale FSM reads. A successful write by a higher-term replacement before invocation establishes a stronger invalidation prefix than loss of connectivity alone. If the old node has not regained authority, success is incompatible with that API responsibility. Nonvoter registration is a candidate mechanism, not the normative source.',alternatives=['Voter-only lease and negative responses may prevent success; keep them running and observe the actual result.'],unresolved=['Real producer/election/Apply/VerifyLeader same-history evidence is required.']))\nbind=dict(id='bind_verify_finish',material_id='src_verify_finish',symbol='VerifyLeader',start_line=848,end_line=870,anchor=dict(material_id='src_verify_api',source_ids=['src_verify_api'],symbol='VerifyLeader',start_line=883,end_line=893,kind='declaration',boundary_complete=True),description='Public verification contract and leader-loop future completion under review.',associations=[dict(claim_id=claim['id'],source_ids=['src_verify_api','src_verify_finish'],rationale='Public contract requires current leadership; leader-loop completion returns the observed future status.')],pending=[])\n# Bind directly to public method to avoid cross-file declaration ambiguity.\nbind.update(material_id='src_verify_api',start_line=883,end_line=893)\njson.dump(m,open('map-verify.json','w'),indent=2)\np=dict(action='obligation',map_path='map-verify.json',sources=sources,question=q,obligation=claim,bindings=[bind],rationale='Membership investigation found an A2 eligibility asymmetry: commitment and lease filter voters, verification registration does not. Preserve that sourced observation without declaring an unsafe decision. Select a bounded real-history check using a replacement leader completed write before old-node verification, retaining all protective workers. This has greater safety value than another local eligibility counter comparison or stale AddVoter documentation mismatch.')\njson.dump(p,open('submission-verify-obligation.json','w'),indent=2)\njsonschema.validate(p,json.load(open('../native-submission.schema.json')));jsonschema.validate(m,json.load(open('../product-schemas.json'))['ConsensusAuditSpec'])\nprint('Validated verification obligation and additive map.')\nPY\n